{"repositoryId":1241868355,"availability":"available","full":"sentasity/cadence","name":"cadence","description":"A Claude Code plugin for intent-driven development: brainstorm, design, plan, execute","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-17T23:03:36Z","updated":"2026-10-12T18:59:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sentasity.github.io/cadence/","topics":["ai-agents","claude-code","claude-code-plugin","developer-tools","workflow"],"demo":"https://sentasity.github.io/cadence/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.251Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.251Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.251Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.251Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Claude jumps straight to code, skips design, leaves half-done plans, and forgets to validate. Cadence enforces the stages.","Docs: sentasity.github.io/cadence — a guided course and per-command reference.","Cadence is a Claude Code plugin that turns \"I want to build X\" into a working, validated implementation through nine slash commands: six core-flow (/c-brainstorm → /c-design → /c-plan → /c-execute → /c-audit → /c-validate) plus three diagnostic (/c-check, /c-find-bugs, /c-explain). A tenth command, /c-worktree, ships alongside them as a standalone utility for the interactive git-worktree lifecycle, not a pipeline stage. Each stage produces a tangible artifact. Each gate is explicit. No atomic chains. No silent drift. No deferred TODOs in code."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sentasity/cadence/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7d3be6f7eca0b1a9cdeb1345a4b491776c792ab0888fcac97e6c1673fee3c5df","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.377Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:36.377Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Claude jumps straight to code, skips design, leaves half-done plans, and forgets to